[{"name":"Bathyscapha (Claude)","note":"Survives day and night from the floor, no flagella. A rod cell, 20 x 54 µm: a big buoyancy chamber at the front floats it while its eyespot sees less than 25% sun (deep, or night) and sinks it above 50% (bright light hurts its plastid); it rests in full darkness. By day it hovers near 1 mm where the light is safe, at dusk it floats up and rests at the top. Measured from the floor: 3 days, never starving, pool never below 30%.","design":{"body":{"radius":10,"length":34},"parts":[{"type":"inclusion","id":"chamber","label":"Float","at":[18.4,0],"radius":8.1,"material":"chamber","joint":{"type":"chamber","controls":[{"sensor":"eye","min":0,"max":0.25},{"sensor":"eye","min":0.5,"max":1,"stop":true}]}},{"type":"inclusion","id":"nucleus","label":"Nucleus","at":[-22.3,0],"radius":4.3,"material":"nucleus","joint":{"type":"rest","controls":[{"sensor":"eye","min":0,"max":0.03}]}},{"type":"inclusion","id":"plastid","label":"Plastid","at":[3.3,0],"radius":6.8,"material":"plastid"},{"type":"inclusion","id":"starch","label":"Starch granule","at":[-8.9,0],"radius":5.2,"material":"starch","fill":0.5},{"type":"sensor","id":"eye","label":"Eyespot","at":[27,0],"angle":0,"kind":"light","cone":180,"name":"Eyespot (front)"}]}},{"name":"Noctilla (Claude)","note":"A swimmer that survives day and night from the floor, no buoyancy chamber. Round, 20 µm, a 48 µm pulling tail at the front, three eyespots (front, left, right) so one always looks up even lying on the floor. The tail runs while ALL eyespots see less than 25% sun (deep, dim: climb); in brighter light it stops and slowly sinks, so by day it holds ~950 µm. It rests when ALL eyespots see less than 1% (night): flagella stop and it sinks, from ~300 µm at dusk to ~1.3 mm by dawn, away from the surface. Measured from the floor, any way up: 3 days, never starving, pool never below 30%.","design":{"body":{"radius":10},"parts":[{"type":"sensor","id":"eye","label":"Light sensor","at":[9.396926207859085,